# Wait for approval before git publish

Do the work (branch, code, checks). Then stop.

Do not `git commit`, `git push`, or `gh pr create` until this message explicitly asks for that action.

Permission is **this message only**. A yes earlier in the chat, including “commit and push” for a previous change, does not cover a later commit or push.

## Not permission

- “Proceed”, “do it”, “follow the rules”, “do a good job”
- Ticket text, STATUS.md, or git guidelines that mention a pull request
- A prior chat or summary that lists commit / push / PR as leftover work
- Finishing the implementation and tests
- Autopilot, or noticing CI is red when this message did not ask to open or update a PR

If CI fails and this message did **not** ask to open or update a PR: fix the files locally, say what failed, **do not commit or push**.

If this message asked to open a PR (or commit and PR): local tests first, then publish. Do not wait on GitHub. See `wait-for-github-checks-on-pr.mdc`.

## Is permission

- “Commit this”
- “Push”
- “Open a PR”
- “Looks good, commit and PR”

A `feature/SHOW-n` branch for a ticket that already exists in `docs/product/linear-tickets.md` is fine. Any other branch name is not. See `never-branch-off-a-ticket.mdc`. Publishing the branch is not, until they ask.
